WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:03.200
-Wh-a-a-a-a-at?!

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:09.334
"Hackney Diamonds" is out now.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:12.501
The new Rolling Stones
album is out now.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:16.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:19.334
And he is on our show tonight.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.000
Last night,
I was very, very lucky.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.167
I got invited to the --
to a secret show, actually.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.634
I went to the album --
It was the album --

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:28.734
What do they call it?
-Release.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.200
-A release party.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.267
I go, "Great. I'll go to see
the album release party to see,

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.567
you know, Mick and Ronnie
and Keith are there."

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.000
I go, "Great."
I go, "Are they playing?"

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.834
They go, "No, no, no, no, no.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.367
No, it's just
an album release party."

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.734
"Okay, cool."
I go, "Well, that's fine.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.033
I'll just go."

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.601
And then I saw you,
and you go -- you're D.J.'ing.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.100
-Yeah.
-And you're there, so I go,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.801
"Oh, cool. That'll be fun.
I'll see Quest.

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.167
It'll be fun to go out there."

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.133
I go in there.
It's a tiny club.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.868
Tiny.
Where was it? Racket.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.100
-Racket.
-On 16th Street, I remember.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.200
It's a beautiful club
but small.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.968
But there's instruments
on stage.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:01.701
-Oh.
-Ooh.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.100
-There's a drum set.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.434
There's guitars.
There's a microphone.

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:09.634
I go, "Uh-oh. I think
something's gonna go down."

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:10.734
All of a sudden,
the lights go out.

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.367
Questlove's
not D.J.'ing anymore.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:14.667
He's sitting where I'm sitting.
I go, "Dude, what's happening?"

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.267
You're like, "Oh, yeah,
it's about to go down."

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.834
They come out,
and it's almost like

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:22.834
♪ Shadow, shadow ♪

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:26.434
I was like, "What?"
It was unbelievable.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:28.601
I was -- honestly, I think --
I'm not kidding.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.501
I don't want to complain.
I think I was too close.

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:34.133
-Yeah.
-Do you think we were too close?

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.234
-That'll never happen
in our lifetime again.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:39.033
-I was too close to the Stones.
-Wow.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.434
-I think it was
a little distracting.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.901
-Like, how close?
-Well, like,

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.267
say I'm here, right?

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.734
This is me.
-Right.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.567
-And he's like --

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.000
And he's like, "Go away,
go away, go away.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.434
[ Gibberish ]

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.968
"Go, go! Stop! Go!
Move out of the way!"

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.601
Like, he couldn't --
I was ruining his mojo.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.934
Mick was out
doing his thing, and...

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.167
And I was just like --

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.734
I was just, like,
sitting, like...

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.067
I was getting --

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.934
I was getting a lap dance
from Mick Jagger.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:07.400
I don't do that.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:11.267
-I don't do that.
But it happened last night.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.334
It was unbelievable.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:16.334
And they came out, and they just
showed everybody how you do it,

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.901
which is like, no tricks,
no computers, no anything.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.300
"Give me a guitar,
give me a microphone.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.701
I'm gonna show you
how to rock out."

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:25.000
And they destroyed.
They were so great.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.300
And at the end, they finished,
and they -- they leave.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.467
And, you know, I don't know
if there's such a thing

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.834
as encores anymore.
Not really, right?

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.667
You kind of know
they're coming out for one more.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:35.834
They have to.
Right?

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.000
The lights turn on,
and you go -- we go home.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.434
Back in the day,
you have to go, "One more..."

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.267
They don't do that anymore.
I'm fine with that.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.000
So I'm playing the game.
I go, "Yeah,"

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.701
but I can --
I can see the lights aren't on,

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.667
so they're gonna come out
for one more.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.100
Not only do they come out
for one more,

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.534
Lady Gaga comes out
with The Rolling Stones.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:58.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.300
I mean, all-timer performance.
-Yes.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.067
All-timer performance.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.767
-Everybody --
Keith was on fire.

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.567
Literally.
Someone lit him on fire.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.467
He was like -- he just played --
He was awesome.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.767
Ronnie Wood and Gaga
just went for it.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.067
Rock 'n' roll.
It was unbelievable.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:17.133
All the new songs
they played, it's great.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:20.234
Anyways, "Hackney Diamonds"
is out officially today.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:25.234
On our show.

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:28.367
He is one of the greatest
guitarists of all time

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.801
in one of the greatest
bands of all time,

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:30.968
The Rolling Stones.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.701
New album, "Hackney Diamonds,"
is out now.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.200
He is here with us tonight.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.934
Keith Richards is on the show
tonight, so that'll be fun.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.968
That'll be cool to see, Keith.
That'll be great.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.734
But we'll get to Keith...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:51.100
♪♪

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.234
Not now. Later.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:55.400
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:00.501
♪♪

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.000
-That was a walk-by.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.734
-Not now.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.300
-He will be on the show,
but not -- not yet.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:12.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.400
How cool is that dude
right there?

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.501
He just --
you know, just walk out.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.334
[ Applause ]

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:19.801
He doesn't care.
He's Keith Richards.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:20.968
He does what he wants.

